  prose(<<~'CANONICAL_PROSE', origin: :published)
    ## Overview
    
    A fire-scarred trade warren in the eastern tunnels of the Nightshelf, dating to the Clever Ice Age and situated adjacent to the colony of ☽'slew Nisaemesius~. Ravium has changed hands twice in living memory — from The Cell, a merchant faction whose ambitions outpaced their defenses, to The Midnight Claws, the syndicate that controlled Nightfall Shelf's shadow economy — and now faces an uncertain future following the Shadow Parliament's dissolution of the Claws under Iudicium∴culum and forfeiture of all their territorial claims. It was the epicenter of The Bra∴conflictu and remains a principal source of fire-core output for both Nightshelf and Aurora Stack heating infrastructure.
    
    ## Physical Character
    
    The main cavern's vaulted ceiling bears scorch-marks in three distinct layers: the original Cell braziers (neat, methodical), the conflagration that consumed them (wild, spiraling), and the Midnight Claws' geometric repairs. The floor is mismatched — native ice, salvaged slate, and in the eastern corner, a patch of dark ice that holds impressions. Those who walk there report seeing Cell merchants burning, Claws operatives stepping over bodies with ledgers in their flippers, orca-blood pooling in channels that were not previously present. The eastern dark ice patch shattered during the Orca Incursion and has not been restored.
    
    Memorial alcoves at junction bends hold lit braziers and names carved into the ice, where workers recite the Vestigium∴moria litany to maintain map privileges. The Cell's old ledgers remain mounted on the north wall, warped by heat and damp. Beside them, someone carved 'VAULIUS KEPT THE FIRE HONEST' into the stone. Beneath it, smaller and older: *Micseleia*. Dagger. The sacred artifact ☽'micseleia' Dagger — forged by Veil-render during the Clever Ice Age — was stored here; Claw warrior Vorolum~ Vigil carried it through the tunnels during the orca breach and used it to defeat the raider Gnarkzund Zaith in the main cavern itself. The Claws never removed either inscription. That restraint invites interpretation.
    
    ## The Corrupted Quarter
    
    Beyond the main cavern lies a sector where The Cell's secondary braziers burned out — blackened spiral scars on every surface, whisper-echoes in voices that should not exist. The walls exude temperatures below what the surrounding geology should permit, consistent with corruption effects documented at other breach-points. Bioluminescent markers have gone dark; the corrupted ice produces frequencies that extinguish them. The corruption sources are catalogued as Freeze-enthrall and Shawl☽ Sun, manifestations of ☽'glacial Crystalline~ Spiral — the Nightshelf time-fracturing magic that fed the worst violence of the Faction Wars.
    
    Midnight Claws operatives sealed the deep-forge access with fire-core morite and crushed quartz during the Orca Incursion — an unsanctioned action no parliamentary body ordered or could have executed. The seal held only seconds before orca raiders breached it. The maintenance channels beyond run Nightshelf-standard gauge, too narrow for orca pursuit. Fire-core veins behind the tunnel walls pulse faintly, cracking under structural stress to spill orange light. Mineral pipes at junction forks can be ruptured to flood corridors with sulfur-heavy water — a defensive measure. Upper galleries provide ambush positions over the main floor.
    
    ## Economic Function and Current Status
    
    Ravium trades krill-oil for crystal-work and salvaged spectralum for deep-mined coal, maintaining links with ☽'moth Silvesiris~, the geothermal springs in the Nightshelf's southern reaches, and The Forum Floe. The last certified quarterly fire-core yield stood at six hundred forty-two units — down ninety-one from the previous cycle, attributed to the orca breach of the deep-forge seal. Senior Signatory Bursar Ingnao shi'Beacon of Aureate certified this figure. All shipments above the third depth require armed escort under chain-of-custody protocols, with escort details posted at Midway Shelf. Quarterly fire-core shipments to Aurora Stack heating stations continued on schedule under Glow-Trader Vemlaus-vel~'s oversight — until the dissolution.
    
    With the Claws dissolved, forge authorization, escort coordination, and thermal vent control lack a governing authority. The Fire Keepers have nominal responsibility. Whether they can hold what the Claws built remains to be demonstrated. The eastern thermal vents went dark after the sub-fourth corridors were sealed, and whoever controls those vents controls who freezes through the next Long Dark.
    
    The old Cell merchants say the place has lost its warmth. They mean something other than temperature.
  CANONICAL_PROSE
  annotation "note_1771585610855_0", anchor: "Claw warrior Vorolum~ Vigil carried it through the tunnels during the orca breach and used it to defeat the raider Gnarkzund Zaith in the main cavern itself", text: "The Foundation Depths preserve coordination orders from the Incursion period that name operatives stationed across every critical eastern tunnel junction — Ravium included. Vorolum~ Vigil may well have killed Gnarkzund Zaith. But one warrior, one legendary dagger, one decisive duel: this is the shape a story takes when no one wants to credit the intelligence network that put the right penguin in the right cavern at the right moment. I wrote the heroic version because it is the version Ravium needs. The coordinated version is in the ice, for whoever comes after me.", type: :skepticism, display: :full
  annotation "note_1771585610855_1", anchor: "The Claws never removed either inscription. That restraint invites interpretation.", text: "And I offered none, which is its own kind of cowardice. But the pattern keeps repeating: the Claws' tunnel-script predates them by two generations; their operational infrastructure was inherited, not built. Leaving Cell inscriptions intact is consistent with an organization that understood the value of appearing to have deeper roots than it possessed. Restraint, or camouflage. I have done similar things with this entry.", type: :commentary, display: :full
  annotation "note_1771585610855_2", anchor: "six hundred forty-two units", text: "Not a round number. After forty-two annotation sessions of flinching at clean figures, an odd specific count from an Aurora bursar is almost enough to make me trust it. Ingnao shi'Beacon's certification stamp also appears on Forum Floe manifests. She counts carefully.", type: :pedantic, display: :popout
  annotation "note_1771585610855_3", anchor: "Freeze-enthrall and Shawl☽ Sun", text: "Freeze-enthrall draws from aurora-light. Aurora-sourced corruption, this deep in Nightshelf territory. The Flipper Accord's containment provisions — including the ones in the drafts no one admits exist — assumed each civilization's corruption stayed on its own side. Ravium's corrupted quarter is evidence that assumption was always wrong.", type: :correction, display: :popout
  annotation "note_1771585610855_4", anchor: "orca-blood pooling in channels that were not previously present", text: "The channels. Not the blood — blood imprints wherever it falls — but channels that the physical cavern does not contain. The dark ice is showing infrastructure from another era layered onto Incursion-period violence. Given that both corruption sources here derive from ☽'glacial Crystalline~ Spiral, which fractures time within ice, this is not standard impression accumulation. The ice's chronology has been broken. Impressions from at least two eras — Incursion and what appears to be pre-Cell construction — are superimposed. I did not flag this in the main text because I could not determine which channels belonged to which period, and I will not guess in print.", type: :temporal, display: :full
